<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 63,761 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 63,761 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 63,761 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Wednesday compared to 90,265 tonnes in the same period on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Wednesday   April 15</p>
<p>    Export cargo		15,761	10,369</p>
<p>    Import cargo		48,000	79,896</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, three ship sailed and four berthed. In the next 24 hours, 10 are expected to sail and 10 are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Tallow		    6,000	 Ocean Meg	    16/4</p>
<p>Sugar		    12,163	 Feng Sheng	   17/4</p>
<p>Soyabean oil	    7,400	 Sophil		 19/4</p>
<p>Palm oil		  8,343	 L. Queen	     19/4</p>
<p>Containers		  555	 CMBT Himalaya	23/4</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
